# card_id_gate.allow — strings that MATCH the card-id shape but are NOT decision cards.
#
# One exact id per line. Comments and blank lines ignored. A NAME, never a pattern:
# a guessed pattern is how a gate quietly stops seeing the thing it was built for.
# Add an entry only after confirming the string is genuinely not a card, and date
# the reason — the next reader needs to know it was measured, not assumed.
#
# Seeded 2026-09-06 22:2x from the measured false positives over 750 staged briefs
# (see card_id_gate.sh's header for the measurement). Both are Azure resource names
# that happened to sit on a line also carrying the word "card".
secuura-demo-rg
secuura-demo-service
# The following are the same infra class, measured in the id-pattern-only run and
# not yet observed on a card-claim line. Listed now because they WILL appear in an
# infra brief eventually, and a false refusal there costs a re-issue for nothing.
secuura-staging-rg
secuura-demo-kv
secuura-staging-kv
# 2026-09-13 Wednesday: fleet/specs/secuura-brief-traps.md is a FILE cited by path in briefs, not a card (gate fired on the s204 brief's PROVENANCE line)
secuura-brief-traps
